\n2026-09-20 | 00:00 | 0\n2026-09-05 | 00:00 | 0\n2026-09-04 | 00:00 | 0\n2026-09-03 | 00:00 | 0\n2026-09-26 | 00:00 | 0\n2026-09-09 | 00:00 | 0\n2026-09-16 | 00:00 | 0\n2026-09-13 | 00:00 | 0\n2026-09-19 | 00:00 | 0\n2026-09-06 | 00:00 | 0","toolCallId":"call_2762819"},{"subagentRunId":"tools:e7ad59da-1d80-c884-cc72-01cf9a3c7295","id":"lc_run--01a14569-2e5f-7a60-bdff-a32232d680ee","role":"assistant","toolCalls":[{"id":"call_1188135","type":"function","function":{"name":"ejecutar_sql","arguments":""}}]},{"subagentRunId":"tools:e7ad59da-1d80-c884-cc72-01cf9a3c7295","id":"call_1188135","role":"tool","content":"10 filas:\ndia | hora | kwh_exportado\n2026-09-20 | 00:00 | 0\n2026-09-05 | 00:00 | 0\n2026-09-04 | 00:00 | 0\n2026-09-03 | 00:00 | 0\n2026-09-26 | 00:00 | 0\n2026-09-09 | 00:00 | 0\n2026-09-16 | 00:00 | 0\n2026-09-13 | 00:00 | 0\n2026-09-19 | 00:00 | 0\n2026-09-06 | 00:00 | 0","toolCallId":"call_1188135"},{"subagentRunId":"tools:e7ad59da-1d80-c884-cc72-01cf9a3c7295","id":"lc_run--01a14569-383e-7342-9a5d-38031366fdc5","role":"assistant","toolCalls":[{"id":"call_1797430","type":"function","function":{"name":"ejecutar_sql","arguments":""}}]},{"subagentRunId":"tools:e7ad59da-1d80-c884-cc72-01cf9a3c7295","id":"call_1797430","role":"tool","content":"10 filas:\ndia | hora | kwh_exportado\n2026-09-01 | 00:00 | 0\n2026-09-01 | 01:00 | 0\n2026-09-01 | 02:00 | 0\n2026-09-01 | 03:00 | 0\n2026-09-01 | 04:00 | 0\n2026-09-01 | 05:00 | 0\n2026-09-01 | 06:00 | 0\n2026-09-01 | 07:00 | 212.5\n2026-09-01 | 08:00 | 455.1\n2026-09-01 | 09:00 | 905.9","toolCallId":"call_1797430"},{"subagentRunId":"tools:e7ad59da-1d80-c884-cc72-01cf9a3c7295","id":"1dcb94c2-ee8a-4fc0-8b17-e08170bfda75","role":"reasoning","content":"**Verifying Calculations and Filtering**\n\nI've confirmed the initial calculation and it's looking clean. Now I'm focusing on validating the total row count: 29 days * 24 hours. The option to filter daytime hours (05:00-19:00) is a key consideration. Heatmaps often benefit from only including the daytime, as solar generation is most relevant during daylight hours, usually starting at 05:00.\n\n\n"},{"subagentRunId":"tools:e7ad59da-1d80-c884-cc72-01cf9a3c7295","id":"lc_run--01a14569-4764-7362-b95a-5c75c8fcd3e6","role":"assistant","toolCalls":[{"id":"call_1685880","type":"function","function":{"name":"ejecutar_sql","arguments":""}}]},{"subagentRunId":"tools:e7ad59da-1d80-c884-cc72-01cf9a3c7295","id":"call_1685880","role":"tool","content":"1 filas:\nmin_hora_con_sol | max_hora_con_sol\n5 | 18","toolCallId":"call_1685880"},{"subagentRunId":"tools:e7ad59da-1d80-c884-cc72-01cf9a3c7295","id":"b10250fc-910d-41bb-a757-78abf801237b","role":"reasoning","content":"**Verifying Availability Details**\n\nI've confirmed that the time frame from 05:00 to 18:00 encompasses the entirety of the generation. I'm now cross-referencing all available data to ensure precision. Specifically, I'm verifying the \"Periodo disponible\" as September 2026, from the 1st to the 29th, a period of 29 days with exported energy data from the border meter.\n\n\n"},{"subagentRunId":"tools:e7ad59da-1d80-c884-cc72-01cf9a3c7295","id":"lc_run--01a14569-590f-71e3-8118-62e32760c9f2","role":"assistant","content":"### Hallazgos\n- **Periodo disponible**: Septiembre de 2026 (datos registrados del 2026-09-01 al 2026-09-29, correspondientes a 29 días de operación).\n- **Total exportado en septiembre**: **154,600 kWh** (154.6 MWh) registrados en el medidor de frontera.\n- **Hora pico habitual**: Las 11:00 AM con un promedio de **769.2 kWh/h** y picos máximos horarios que superan los **1,000 kWh/h** entre las 11:00 y las 13:00. La ventana efectiva de generación solar va desde las 05:00 hasta las 18:00.\n- **Días de máxima generación**:\n  - **2026-09-09**: 8,908 kWh exportados (irradiancia POA: 8.89 kWh/m²).\n  - **2026-09-10**: 7,954 kWh exportados.\n  - **2026-09-12**: 7,944 kWh exportados.\n- **Anomalías y días de menor generación**:\n  - **2026-09-23 y 2026-09-24**: 0 kWh exportados a pesar de alta disponibilidad solar (POA > 6.8 kWh/m²), indicando una desconexión o falla total de planta/frontera.\n  - **2026-09-18**: Solo 48.1 kWh exportados con irradiancia óptima (8.26 kWh/m²).\n  - **2026-09-27**: 1,132 kWh exportados debido a cobertura nubosa (POA de 3.89 kWh/m²).\n\n---\n\n### Consultas para graficar\n\n#### Mapa de calor de generación por hora y día (Septiembre 2026)\n- **Qué muestra**: Distribución horaria (05:00 a 18:00) de la energía exportada (kWh) para cada día de septiembre de 2026.\n- **Tipo sugerido**: `mapa_calor`\n- **Columna X**: `dia` (fecha en formato YYYY-MM-DD)\n- **Columna Y**: `hora` (hora del día en formato HH:00)\n- **Columna Valor**: `kwh_exportado` (kWh)\n\n```sql\nSELECT \n    to_char(hora AT TIME ZONE 'America/Bogota', 'YYYY-MM-DD') AS dia,\n    to_char(hora AT TIME ZONE 'America/Bogota', 'HH24:00') AS hora,\n    round(COALESCE(kwh_frontera, 0)::numeric, 2) AS kwh_exportado\nFROM analitica.v_energia_horaria\nWHERE hora >= '2026-09-01 00:00:00-05' AND hora < '2026-10-01 00:00:00-05'\n  AND EXTRACT(HOUR FROM hora AT TIME ZONE 'America/Bogota') BETWEEN 5 AND 18\nORDER BY hora AT TIME ZONE 'America/Bogota' ASC;\n```"}]}

